</style><script src="chrome-extension://liecbddmkiiihnedobmlmillhodjkdmb/js/recordConsoleEvents.js"></script></head><body><div class="page" id="page"><div class="title">Foothill College Workforce Pathway : Manufacturing Technician</div>
<div class="byline">By Dayone Koo · kallipolis.us · June 21, 2026</div>
<div class="subtitle">Foothill College is committed to training students to fill critical roles in the region's advanced manufacturing sector. This report examines how Foothill College programs support the Manufacturing Technician role and how those programs align with other schools in the BACCC to meet regional labor-market demand.</div>
<h1>Regional Occupational Demand</h1>
<p>The U.S. Department of Labor's O*NET system maps the title <b>Manufacturing Technician</b> to these standard occupational classifications, supported by Foothill College programs. According to the Centers of Excellence, these occupations roughly represent 410 openings a year in the Bay Area labor market.&nbsp;</p>
<table class="dem"><tbody><tr><th>SOC</th><th>Occupation</th><th class="n">Openings / yr</th><th class="n">5-yr growth</th><th class="n">Median salary</th></tr><tr><td>51-9141</td><td>Semiconductor Processing Technicians</td><td class="n">180</td><td class="n">+3.2%</td><td class="n">$49,340</td></tr><tr><td>17-3026</td><td>Industrial Engineering Technologists and Technicians</td><td class="n">150</td><td class="n">+7.6%</td><td class="n">$79,950</td></tr><tr><td>17-3024</td><td>Electro-Mechanical and Mechatronics Technologists and Technicians</td><td class="n">80</td><td class="n">−1.4%</td><td class="n">$78,280</td></tr><tr class="tot"><td></td><td>Total regional demand</td><td class="n">≈ 410</td><td class="n">—</td><td class="n">—</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p><br></p><p>Prominent employers in the region have opened live job postings listed on CareerOneStop under the <b>Manufacturing Technician </b>title.&nbsp;</p>
<table class="live"><colgroup><col style="width:40%"><col style="width:17%"><col style="width:43%"></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="lsoc">Occupation</th><th>Employer</th><th>Live posting</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="lc1"><td class="lsoc">Semiconductor Processing Technicians<span>SOC 51-9141</span></td><td class="lemp">Western Digital</td><td class="ltit"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.careeronestop.org/Toolkit/Jobs/find-jobs-details.aspx?keyword=51-9141.00&amp;location=94022&amp;radius=25&amp;pagesize=250&amp;curPage=1&amp;fc=1&amp;jvid=3a2661a8ee924549b4919d7c011391388003&amp;detailpage=true">Wafer Manufacturing Process Technician ↗</a></td></tr><tr class="lc2"><td class="lsoc">Industrial Engineering Technologists and Technicians<span>SOC 17-3026</span></td><td class="lemp">Applied Materials</td><td class="ltit"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.careeronestop.org/Toolkit/Jobs/find-jobs-details.aspx?keyword=17-3026.00&amp;location=94022&amp;radius=25&amp;pagesize=250&amp;curPage=1&amp;fc=1&amp;jvid=8c9823b4e0f04ac89f88990eccee32388003&amp;detailpage=true">Electrical Engineering Technician IV ↗</a></td></tr><tr class="lc3"><td class="lsoc">Electro-Mechanical and Mechatronics Technologists and Technicians<span>SOC 17-3024</span></td><td class="lemp">J&amp;J Family of Companies</td><td class="ltit"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.careeronestop.org/Toolkit/Jobs/find-jobs-details.aspx?keyword=17-3024.00&amp;location=94022&amp;radius=25&amp;pagesize=250&amp;curPage=1&amp;fc=1&amp;jvid=dfd0b0e608344861a2f3a7c7fa2df4de8003&amp;detailpage=true">Manufacturing Tech III – Surgical Robotics ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table>
<h1>Occupational Competencies</h1>
<table class="cmpgrid"><tbody><tr><th class="c1h">51-9141</th><th class="c2h">17-3026</th><th class="c3h">17-3024</th></tr><tr class="sec"><td colspan="3">Description</td></tr><tr class="descrow"><td>Perform any or all of the following functions in the manufacture of electronic semiconductors: load semiconductor material into furnace; saw formed ingots into segments; load individual segment into crystal growing chamber and monitor controls; locate crystal axis in ingot using x-ray equipment and saw ingots into wafers; and clean, polish, and load wafers into series of special purpose furnaces, chemical baths, and equipment used to form circuitry and change conductive properties.</td><td>Apply engineering theory and principles to problems of industrial layout or manufacturing production, usually under the direction of engineering staff.</td><td>Operate, test, maintain, or adjust unmanned, automated, servomechanical, or electromechanical equipment.</td></tr><tr class="sec"><td colspan="3">Knowledge</td></tr><tr><td>Production and Processing</td><td>Mechanical</td><td>Mechanical</td></tr><tr><td>Chemistry</td><td>Engineering and Technology</td><td>Engineering and Technology</td></tr><tr><td>Public Safety and Security</td><td>Physics</td><td>Computers and Electronics</td></tr><tr><td>Computers and Electronics</td><td>Design</td><td>Production and Processing</td></tr><tr class="sec"><td colspan="3">Skills</td></tr><tr><td>Equipment Maintenance</td><td>Technology Design</td><td>Repairing</td></tr><tr><td>Operations Monitoring</td><td>Operations Analysis</td><td>Installation</td></tr><tr><td>Quality Control Analysis</td><td>Repairing</td><td>Troubleshooting</td></tr><tr><td>Troubleshooting</td><td>Science</td><td>Operations Monitoring</td></tr><tr class="sec"><td colspan="3">Abilities</td></tr><tr><td>Rate Control</td><td>Inductive Reasoning</td><td>Control Precision</td></tr><tr><td>Arm-Hand Steadiness</td><td>Number Facility</td><td>Arm-Hand Steadiness</td></tr><tr><td>Multilimb Coordination</td><td>Mathematical Reasoning</td><td>Finger Dexterity</td></tr><tr><td>Control Precision</td><td>Deductive Reasoning</td><td>Reaction Time</td></tr><tr class="sec"><td colspan="3">Technology</td></tr><tr><td>Industrial control software</td><td>Enterprise application integration software</td><td>Object or component oriented development software</td></tr><tr><td>Development environment software</td><td>Process mapping and design software</td><td>Computer aided design CAD software</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Cloud-based data access and sharing software</td><td>Program testing software</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Development environment software</td><td>Computer aided manufacturing CAM software</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h1>College Program Alignment &amp; Supply</h1>
<p>How member-college programs across the consortium feed each occupation, derived from the TOP–CIP–SOC crosswalk published by the Centers of Excellence.</p>
